  "rule": "Each 3-cell L emitter (a 2x2 box with one corner missing) fires a diagonal ray from its tip, pointing away from the missing corner, painted in its own colour. The ray stops at the border or just before hitting a reflector bar head-on. Whenever a ray cell is orthogonally adjacent to a reflector, the ray adopts the reflector colour from that cell on. It also reverses its vertical component (reflector above or below) or its horizontal component (reflector left or right). Chained bounces follow the same rule.",
  "scope": "Supported: grids of 12-30 rows and columns, 1-4 emitters with any of the 4 diagonal directions, and 0-6 reflector bars that are horizontal or vertical with length 1-3. Colours are drawn independently from 1-9. Scenes include multi-bounce chains, head-on stops and distractor bars. Deliberately not supported: rays that cross each other or themselves, rays that pass over L cells, cells that touch two reflectors at once, same-colour objects that touch each other, and non-terminating or looping rays. Each of these makes the result depend on painting order or on the object-segmentation convention. The canonical fixtures are rebuilt from explicit emitter and bar parameters. An additional native parallel branch constructs 3..14 adjacent differently coloured emitters on the top border, sharing a downward diagonal direction. It has no reflectors or ray crossings.",
  "constraints": [
    "General scenes separate all objects by an empty 8-neighbourhood. Dense parallel scenes permit touching emitters only with distinct neighbouring colours.",
    "The L tip is not on the border. General rays paint at least two cells; dense parallel rays paint at least one before exiting.",
    "Every ray terminates, by leaving the grid or meeting a reflector head-on, within height+width steps.",
    "No ray cell is orthogonally adjacent to more than one reflector cell.",
    "Ray cells are pairwise disjoint across all rays, are not repeated within a ray, and never cover any object cell.",
    "When bars exist, at least one bounce occurs in the scene.",
    "The background is 0 and dominates the grid."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Ray crossings and overlaps are excluded, so painting-order effects are never exercised.",
    "Reflectors are only straight bars of length 1-3; other reflector shapes are not generated.",
    "General scenes separate all objects. The dense parallel branch allows adjacent differently coloured emitters, all pointing down with a shared horizontal direction; fully general adjacent-emitter arrangements are not sampled.",
    "General scenes require termination within height+width steps, matching the saved solver. Failed rejection sampling raises without substituting a canned scene."
  ],
